# ── AI providers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kaagaz needs ONE of these to work. More means automatic failover, and
# the order is fixed in app/ai/client.py: OpenRouter -> Groq -> NVIDIA NIM.
#
# A provider with no key is skipped without being called. A provider that is
# configured but out of credit or rate-limited is tripped out of the rotation
# for 5 minutes rather than paying a failed round trip on every request.
#
# Which one is best for what:
#   OPENROUTER  Best quality for the structured research prompt (gpt-4o-mini).
#               Needs a funded key; a free-tier key with no credit always 402s.
#   GROQ        Very fast, and has a usable free tier. Model list is discovered
#               from the API rather than hardcoded, so Groq's rotating
#               catalogue cannot break it.
#   NVIDIA_NIM  Works with a free key, slowest of the three. Good last resort.
#
# Only the generation step uses these. The web-search step prefers a keyless
# path (see app/research/search.py) and needs no key at all.

# Optional. Primary. ~$0.00005 per generation call.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional. Fast, and free-tier friendly.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional. Third fallback.
NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY=

# ── App ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
FLASK_ENV=development
SECRET_KEY=change-me-in-production
